1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,516
Di sebuah pabrik di Karawang,

2
00:00:02,620 --> 00:00:05,446
satu mobil keluar dari jalur kira-kira

3
00:00:05,466 --> 00:00:06,416
tiap seratus detik.

4
00:00:06,881 --> 00:00:09,399
Tapi membuat satu mobil butuh berjam-jam.

5
00:00:09,899 --> 00:00:11,210
Kuncinya bukan kerja cepat,

6
00:00:11,230 --> 00:00:13,547
tapi banyak mobil dikerjakan bersamaan

7
00:00:13,567 --> 00:00:15,729
di satu jalur yang terus bergerak.

8
00:00:16,229 --> 00:00:19,865
Pertama, lembaran baja dipres jadi panel.

9
00:00:20,058 --> 00:00:22,081
Robot lalu mengelas ribuan titik sampai

10
00:00:22,101 --> 00:00:23,071
jadi rangka bodi.

11
00:00:23,241 --> 00:00:25,219
Bodi dicelup cat antikarat bermuatan

12
00:00:25,239 --> 00:00:27,274
listrik, dilapisi cat warna,

13
00:00:27,294 --> 00:00:28,636
lalu dipanggang di oven.

14
00:00:29,141 --> 00:00:30,465
Di jalur perakitan,

15
00:00:30,485 --> 00:00:31,687
pintu dilepas dulu,

16
00:00:31,986 --> 00:00:35,061
lalu bodi disatukan dengan mesin dan suspensi.

17
00:00:35,231 --> 00:00:38,147
Pekerja dan robot memasang ribuan komponen

18
00:00:38,223 --> 00:00:39,391
yang datang tepat waktu.

19
00:00:39,891 --> 00:00:42,025
Sebelum keluar, mobil disiram air untuk

20
00:00:42,045 --> 00:00:44,401
cek kebocoran dan diuji di atas roller.

21
00:00:44,571 --> 00:00:47,439
Kalau ada masalah, pekerja bisa menarik

22
00:00:47,459 --> 00:00:49,291
tali andon dan menghentikan lini.

23
00:00:49,794 --> 00:00:53,210
Jadi ribuan mobil lahir dari ritme, bukan terburu-buru.

24
00:00:53,381 --> 00:00:54,721
Ini AUDIRA Explained.
